{"type":"text","timestamp":1794527791979,"sessionID":"ses_e2dd11478ffewTC2lNQ9TA6Xhv","part":{"id":"prt_1d230ffa2002mjVUNGXMgQ78nh","sessionID":"ses_e2dd11478ffewTC2lNQ9TA6Xhv","messageID":"msg_1d230f80c001x64BOgIArh2tqM","type":"text","text":"T022 complete.\n\n**File written**\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/cli-degraded-command-contract.vitest.ts` (new, untracked)\n\nIt imports the exported `degradedRecommendations` from `../skill-advisor-cli.js` and covers the two required shapes: a typed `/speckit:save this session` prompt over a `command-speckit-save` entry keeps `command: '/speckit:save'` and `policy: 'start'`, and `create a readme for the utils folder` over `sk-doc` plus `command-create-readme` collapses to one `sk-doc` entry with no `command` property.\n\n**Verify (in `ADV`)**\n```\n$ npx vitest run tests/cli-degraded-command-contract.vitest.ts\n\n RUN  v4.1.12 /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  2 passed (2)\n   Start at  00:56:19\n   Duration  114ms (transform 43ms, setup 20ms, import 34ms, tests 2ms, environment 0ms)\n```\n\nFirst run failed on an over-strict `kind: 'skill'` assertion for the `sk-doc` entry (that entry has no command row, so it is pushed without a `kind` field). I narrowed the assertion to what the task specifies (`sk-doc`, no `command`) and reran green.\n\n**Nothing left undone.** The `- [ ] T022` checkbox was not ticked, no other file was touched, and no git state was changed. The untracked file above is the only workspace change from this task.","time":{"start":1794527788962,"end":1794527791979}}}
